{
  "schema": "ancora.parity.scenario.v1",
  "id": "s12-order-upkeep",
  "title": "Order and priority upkeep (D13): classification priorities and template order, appended, moved and renumbered",
  "notes": [
    "Issue #70, D13 (legacy-parity-inventory.md PAR-019, PAR-020, PAR-035; SQL cases 111, 112, 144). One plan and period (5 days x 3 slots), one group.",
    "Legacy side: the priority and the order come from the hidden fields of the new-record forms (get_form_new_clasifact, get_form_new_plantilla: count + 1); the edits use the legacy arrows (set_ClasifAct_subeprioridad / _bajaprioridad, custom_SubePlantilla / custom_BajaPlantilla) and the delete handlers. Drupal side: OrderUpkeep, the same moves and the entity deletes.",
    "Edits: template AX (order 2, no assignment) is deleted, so A2 and A3 move to 2 and 3; A3 moves up, A1 moves down: the order is A3, A1, A2. Classification C1 moves down, C3 moves up, C2 is deleted: C3 = 1, C1 = 2. With respetar_orden the run places the templates on days 1, 2, 3 in that order.",
    "Rows are matched by natural key, so a template is named after the scenario record with its FINAL order (order 1 = A1, 2 = AX, 3 = A2) on both sides."
  ],
